  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 400 PM MST Wed Nov 18 2026/ The upper level low that \ncaused the rain/snow yesterday is slow exiting the area late this \nafternoon. A few light snow showers are possible this evening, \nmostly north of Highway 2 from Havre to Harlem. Some patchy fog is\npossible by Thu morning, but with increasing cloud cover the \nprobability is on the low side.\n\nLight snow showers start to increase by Thu afternoon over far\nSouthwest MT, mostly around the West Yellowstone and Monida Pass\narea. Expect a better chance for snowfall Friday night into\nSaturday, as an upper level low moves southward from Canada\nthrough the CWA. \n\nAfternoon temperatures will be a bit on the cold side, with many\nareas about 10 degrees or more below normal for afternoon highs.\n\nBy early next week, an upper level ridge will start to build over\nthe northern Rockies. This will allow for a very slow warming\ntrend to begin, but also for mostly dry conditions for much of\nnext week. Brusda",
